################################################################################
# .AGENTS FILE
# MintMuseily repository guidance
# Repository: 940smiley/mintmuseily
# Updated: 2026-09-29

## 1. Project overview
Project: MintMuseily
Description: Web3 dApp for music generation with NFT minting
Repo URL: https://github.com/940smiley/mintmuseily
Status: MVP / prototype stage
Main tech: Foundry + Solidity + Next.js + React + TypeScript + wagmi + RainbowKit

## 2. Language composition
Languages by code size:
- Solidity: dominant codebase; used for NFT contract logic
- Python: supporting script/tooling
- TypeScript: web app code and config typing
- JavaScript: config and tool files
- CSS: utility/layout styling

## 3. Repository structure
- mintmuseily-contracts/
  - src/: contract source files
  - test/: contract tests
  - script/: deployment helpers
- mintmuseily-web/
  - src/app/: app routes and pages
  - src/components/: UI and web3 components
  - public/: static assets
- forge/
  - Foundry tooling and library config
- .github/, .vscode/
  - support and editor config

## 4. Current implementation status
Completed:
- ERC721 NFT contract with single and batch mint functions
- Wallet connection and wallet UI
- Sepolia testnet integration
- Mint UX with success modal
- Foundry-based contract project structure

Still missing or incomplete:
- Music generation workflow
- Metadata/IPFS pipeline
- Strong production validation
- Admin roles and access controls
- Deployment documentation
- Automated CI and test coverage

## 5. Open issues / PRs
Open Issues: 13
Open dependency PRs: multiple Dependabot updates
Primary upgrade areas:
- Next.js major version review
- wagmi/viem compatibility review
- eslint / supporting package updates
- security-related dependency bumps

## 6. Immediate tasks
Priority 1
- [ ] Investigate open issues and categorize them
- [ ] Implement actual music generation flow
- [ ] Add metadata/IPFS support for NFTs
- [ ] Expand contract test coverage
- [ ] Improve error handling and UX

Priority 2
- [ ] Review and validate dependency updates before merge
- [ ] Add environment/deployment docs
