## 7. Recommended upgrades and improvements
Smart contracts
- Add pausable control and access control roles
- Add royalty support (ERC2981)
- Add tokenURI/baseURI support for metadata
- Add events for better mint tracking
- Review upgrade path for future contract improvements

Frontend
- Improve error boundaries and state handling
- Add loading/spinner and success states where needed
- Add transaction hashes and Etherscan links
- Review wallet persistence and retry logic
- Improve onboarding UX for first-time users

Infrastructure
- Add GitHub Actions CI
- Add lint/test/build verification
- Add contract static analysis (Slither/MythX)
- Add staging/testnet deploy flow
- Create docs for environment variables and setup

## 8. Standards for agents and bots
- Keep code secure, well-documented, and testable
- Log all work to agents.log
- Update .agents when task status changes
- Keep commits small and focused
- Validate contract and UI changes before finalizing
- Prefer minimal, deterministic changes

## 9. Mandatory logging requirements
All agent activity must be recorded in agents.log using the format:
[YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ] [AGENT_NAME] [ACTION] [DETAILS]

## 10. Notes
The repo is in a promising MVP state but still lacks the major product-level feature: the actual music generation + metadata lifecycle. The next meaningful progress should focus on product completeness, testing, and deployment readiness rather than cosmetic polish alone.
